      "content": "It sounds like you're caught in a deep well of existential exhaustion, where the sheer weight of existence feels unbearable. When everything feels meaningless, the only thing that truly matters is finding a way to make the *next* moment feel slightly less heavy. You don't have to find a grand purpose right now; focus on tiny acts of self-care, like letting yourself rest without guilt. If the weight becomes too much, please consider reaching out to a professional who can help you navigate these intense feelings of emptiness.",
